1. e4 e6 2. d4 c5 $6 {What is correct now according to the Golden Opening Principles?}
(2... d5 {is the only correct move.}) 3. d5 $1 {The pawn becomes weak, but the aim is to restrict Black's pieces so that White's own pieces are strong.} (3. Nf3 {is okay as a move, but it justifies Black's move c5.}
cxd4 4. Nxd4 {Transposes to the Sicilian Defense.}) (3. Be3 $6 {is worse than Nf3.} cxd4 4. Bxd4 Nc6 {You want to keep the bishop, but then it would have to lose a tempo...}) (3. c3 d5 {is okay for Black.}) 3... e5 $2 {Black loses another tempo in the opening.} (3... exd5 4. exd5 d6 {would now be correct.}) 4. f4 $5 {not necessary, but strong.} ({Typical moves would be} 4. Nf3
) ({or} 4. c4 {with a positional space advantage later.}) 4... d6 (4... exf4 5.
Bxf4 {develops White's position.}) 5. Nf3 {develops while supporting the center.} (5. Bc4 $2 {is poor development because the bishop is staring at d5.}) 5... Bg4 6. fxe5 Bxf3 $2 {Contradicts the development principle. Black exchanges without reason and develops White's queen. Black could at least have waited until h3.} 7. Qxf3
dxe5 8. Bb5+ {Entwicklung} Nd7 9. Nc3 {Entwicklung} Ngf6 10. Bg5 {Entwicklung}
Be7 11. d6 $3 {An active move with a brilliant idea.} Bxd6 12. O-O-O {Black resigned here.} ({Other moves based on the same idea also win, for example:} 12. Bxf6
Qxf6 13. Qxf6 gxf6 14. O-O-O Ke7 15. Bxd7 Kxd7 16. Nb5) (12. Bxd7+ Qxd7 13.
Bxf6 gxf6 14. Qxf6 {is technically winning as well, but the material advantage is not yet as large.} Rg8 15. O-O-O Be7 $16) (12. Nd5 Qa5+ {spoils White's idea.} 13.
Nc3 {although thanks to Rd1 it is still winning.}) 12... Be7 (12... Qe7 {There are two winning methods here.} 13. Nd5 {The knight on f6 is pinned.} (13. Bxd7+ Qxd7 (13... Kxd7
14. Nb5 {The bishop on d6 is pinned.}) 14. Bxf6 gxf6 15. Qxf6) 13... Qe6 14. Bxf6 gxf6
15. Nxf6+ {The knight on d7 is pinned as well.}) (12... a6 13. Bxd7+ Qxd7 (13... Kxd7 14.
Rxd6+ $1 (14. Rd2 {also wins, but leads to the same thing.}) 14... Kxd6
15. Rd1+ Kc7 16. Rxd8 Raxd8 17. Bxf6 gxf6 18. Nd5+) 14. Bxf6 gxf6 15. Qxf6 {
Doppelangriff} Rg8 16. Rxd6) 13. Bxf6 Bxf6 14. Rxd7 1-0

