1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 $6 3. d4 Bg4 $2 4. dxe5 Bxf3 {forced, even though it develops White's position.} (4... dxe5 5. Qxd8+ Kxd8 6. Nxe5 {An extra pawn for White.}) 5. Qxf3 dxe5
6. Bc4 Nf6 7. Qb3 {Double attack. Black now loses a pawn.} Qe7 (7...
Nxe4 $4 8. Bxf7+ Kd7 9. Qe6#) 8. Nc3 $5 {White decides against taking the pawn on b7 and chooses the attack instead.} (8. Qxb7 {Black would have planned} Qb4+ {after which it would "only" be an endgame with an extra pawn.}) 8... c6 (8... Qb4 9. Bxf7+) 9. Bg5 {Black can do little.} b5 (9... Nbd7 10. Qxb7) (9... h6 10. Bxf6 gxf6 (
10... Qxf6 $2 11. Qxb7) 11. O-O-O {and once again Black cannot make progress, for example:} Bg7
12. Bxf7+ $1 Qxf7 13. Rd8+ Kxd8 14. Qxf7 $18) 10. Nxb5 $3 {more for beauty than for strength.} cxb5 11. Bxb5+ Nbd7 12. O-O-O {Now all of White's pieces join the attack.} Rd8 13. Rxd7 $1 Rxd7 14. Rd1 Qe6 {steps out of the pin and continues to defend d7.} (14... Qb4 15. Bxf6 gxf6 {White does not have to enter the endgame, although that would also be winning.} (15... Qxb3 16. Bxd7#) 16.
Bxd7+ Kd8 (16... Ke7 17. Qxb4+) 17. Qxf7) 15. Bxd7+ Nxd7 (15... Qxd7 16. Qb8+ {White wins simply because of the material advantage.}) 16. Qb8+ $3 {again for beauty.} Nxb8 17. Rd8# 1-0

