1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Qf6 $2 {The queen was moved too early.} 3. Nc3 {already threatens Nd5, so Black has to spend time dealing with it.} c6 4. d4 $1 exd4 5. e5 $5 (5. Nxd4 {is not worse.} Bc5 6. Be3) 5... Qg6 6. Bd3 $5 {White simply wants to sacrifice.} (6.
Qxd4 {would be my choice, even with a small trap.} Qxc2 7. Bd3 {The queen is trapped.}) 6... Qxg2 (6... Qh5 7. Ne2) 7. Rg1 Qh3 8. Rg3 Qh5 9. Rg5 Qh3 {White has an enormous lead in development for the pawn.} 10. Bf1 ({Another option would be} 10.
Bf5 Qh6 11. Qxd4) (10. Nxd4 Qxh2 11. Qf3 {with queenside castling, Bc4, ...}) 10...
Qe6 11. Nxd4 Qe7 12. Ne4 {[%cal Re4d6] weak square on d6.} (12. Nf5 $2 {drops a pawn.} Qxe5+ 13. Be3 g6) 12... h6 13. Nf5 $4 (13. Nd6+ Kd8
14. Rf5 {would be good.}) 13... Qe6 $4 (13... Qxe5 {White surely saw this.}
14. Nfd6+ {[%cal Rg5e5]} Bxd6 15. Rxe5+ Bxe5 16. Nd6+ $18) (13... Qb4+ {[%cal Rb4e4,Rb4e1] But both players missed this. With the intermediate check, Black wins immediately.} 14. Nc3 (14. Bd2 Qxe4+) 14... hxg5) 14. Nfd6+ (14. Rg4 $4 {Do not move the rook away; that loses material.} Qxf5) (14. Bc4 $2 {Good idea, but it does not work.} d5 $1 (14... Qxc4 $140 15. Nfd6+) 15. exd6 Qxe4+) 14... Bxd6
15. Nxd6+ Kd8 16. Bc4 {Continue with active moves first.} Qe7 (16... Qh3 {Exercise: find White's win.} 17. Nxf7+ Kc7 18. Qd6+ Kb6 19. Be3+ Ka5 (19... Qxe3+ 20.
fxe3 hxg5 21. Nxh8) 20. Qa3# (20. e6+ hxg5)) 17. Nxf7+ Kc7 18. Qd6+ $1 {not because of the queen trade, but because Black is actually getting checkmated.} Qxd6 (18... Kb6 19.
Be3+ Ka5 {Exercise: find a winning continuation.} 20. b4+ Ka4 21. Bb3+ Kb5 (21... Ka3
22. Bc1#) 22. a4+ Ka6 23. b5+ (23. Bc4+ b5 24. axb5+ Kb7 {is not mate, but wins a large amount of material.}) 23... Ka5 24. Bd2+ (24. Qc7+ b6 25. Bd2+ Qb4 {
Damengewinn}) 24... Kb6 25. a5+ Kxb5 26. Qd3+ Kc5 27. Qc4#) 19. exd6+ Kb6 {Be careful for a moment: White's rook is still hanging.} 20. Be3+ (20. Nxh8 hxg5) 20... c5
21. Bxc5+ Ka5 (21... Kc6 22. Nd8#) 22. Rg3 (22. b4+ {also leads to mate.} Ka4
23. Bb3+ Ka3 (23... Kb5 24. a4+ Ka6 25. Bc4+ b5 26. axb5+ Kb7 27. Nd8#) 24. Rg4
{with mate coming soon.}) (22. Rxg7 {alternatively wins Black's rook without losing White's own rook.}) 22... b5 23. Ra3# 1-0

