1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 {Evans Gambit} Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 6. d4 exd4
7. O-O Bxc3 $2 {This is too greedy.} 8. Nxc3 dxc3 {Black is three full pawns up, but has no development at all.} 9. Ba3 (9. Qb3 {would be the more precise move order.} Qf6 (9... Qe7 10. Ba3 d6 11. e5 $1 {opens the position.}
Nxe5 $140 $2 12. Nxe5 Qxe5 13. Rfe1) (9... Nh6 {does not work here, unlike in the game.} 10. Bxh6) 10. e5 $1 Nxe5 11. Nxe5 Qxe5 12. Bxf7+) 9... d6
10. Qb3 Nh6 11. Qxc3 Qf6 ({Black has been given the chance to save the game, but does not take it.} 11... O-O) 12. e5 $1 dxe5 (12... Nxe5 13. Nxe5 O-O $3 {would have saved Black.}) 13. Rfe1 {The game is now critical. White is three pawns down, so White has to deliver mate or may as well resign.} Bd7 {Black is clever and castles queenside.} 14. Rab1 O-O-O {Can the attack continue?}
15. Ba6 $1 (15. Qb2 b6 {deswegen zuerst Ba6}) 15... Na5 {Black misjudges the variations.} (15... bxa6 16. Qb3 Bg4 17. Qb7+ Kd7 18. Rbd1+ Ke8 19.
Rxd8+ Nxd8 20. Qxc7 Bxf3 21. Rxe5+ Ne6 22. Qc8+ Qd8 23. Rxe6+ {and wins.})
16. Rec1 (16. Qxa5 $2 Qxa6 $19) 16... Bc6 17. Qxa5 bxa6 18. Qxa6+ Kd7 19. Rxc6
$1 Qf5 (19... Qxc6 20. Nxe5+) 20. Rxc7+ $1 Ke8 21. Qc6+ Qd7 22. Rb8 $5 {unnecessarily plays for beauty.} (22. Rxd7 Rxd7 23. Rb8# {would be enough.}) 22... Qxc6 23.
Re7+ Kf8 24. Rxd8+ Qe8 25. Rexe8# 1-0

